<% closure = site_closure %>
<% date = ->(day) { day.strftime("%B %-d, %Y") } %>
<% content_for :title, closure.closed? ? "Dabble Me has closed" : "Dabble Me is closing" %>

<section class="py-12 lg:py-20">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
      <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl sm:text-5xl tracking-tight">
        <%= closure.closed? ? "Dabble Me has closed" : "Dabble Me is closing" %>
      </h1>

      <div class="mt-8 space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
        <% if closure.closed? %>
          <p>Dabble Me's last day was <%= date.(closure.closes_on) %>. The journal emails have stopped and the site is closed.</p>
          <p>
            <span class="text-primary font-medium">Your journal is still yours.</span>
            You can sign in and export all of it until <%= date.(closure.deletes_on) %>. After that day every journal is permanently deleted.
          </p>
        <% else %>
          <p>Dabble Me is closing. Its last day is <%= date.(closure.closes_on) %>, and from today it isn't taking new accounts or new subscriptions.</p>
          <p>
            <span class="text-primary font-medium">If you have a journal here, please export it.</span>
            Everything keeps working through <%= date.(closure.closes_on) %>. After that day the site and the journal emails stop.
            You can still sign in to export until <%= date.(closure.deletes_on) %>, and after that day every journal is permanently deleted.
          </p>
        <% end %>

        <p>
          <a href="<%= export_entries_path %>" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-olive-900 px-6 py-3 text-base font-medium text-white hover:bg-olive-800 transition-colors">Export your journal</a>
        </p>

        <p>
          You'll be asked to sign in. Choose to export everything, and you'll get an email with a link to a ZIP file holding all of your entries and photos.
          It opens in any web browser and needs no account.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you pay for PRO, you won't be charged again. To have your journal deleted sooner, sign in and delete your account from
          <a href="<%= edit_user_registration_path %>" class="text-accent hover:text-primary underline">your settings</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          Questions go to <a href="mailto:hello@<%= ENV['MAIN_DOMAIN'] %>" class="text-accent hover:text-primary underline">hello@<%= ENV['MAIN_DOMAIN'] %></a>.
          Dabble Me's code stays <a href="https://github.com/parterburn/dabble.me" class="text-accent hover:text-primary underline">open source</a> for anyone who wants to run their own.
        </p>
        <p>Thank you for writing here.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
